# Production builds ship with no API key, on purpose.
#
# Vite inlines every VITE_* variable into the JavaScript bundle as a literal string.
# A key set at build time is therefore readable by anyone who opens the site or unzips
# the APK — it is not a secret once it is built. An earlier APK did carry one.
#
# This file overrides .env for production, so `npm run build` and `npm run apk` are
# always keyless. The tutor then runs on its 105 offline topics, and anyone who wants
# the language model pastes their own key into Settings, where it stays in their own
# browser's localStorage and is never bundled or transmitted anywhere but the provider.
#
# For a keyed build during local development, use `npm run dev`, which reads .env.

VITE_LLM_API_KEY=
